aumann</surname><given-names>A.</given-names></name><name><surname>Kaupp</surname><given-names>U.B.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Probing the transmembrane topology of cyclic nucleotide&#x02013;gated ion channels with a gene fusion approach</article-title><source>Proc. Natl. Acad. Sci. USA.</source><volume>92</volume><year>1995</year><fpage>7425</fpage><lpage>7429</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7543681</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="Holmgrenetal1996"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Holmgren</surname><given-names>M.</given-names></name><name><surname>Liu</surname><given-names>Y.</given-names></name><name><surname>Xu</surname><given-names>Y.</given-names></name><name><surname>Yellen</surname><given-names>G.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>On the use of thiol-modifying agents to determine channel topology</article-title><source>Neuropharmacology.</source><volume>35</volume><year>1996</year><fpage>797</fpage><lpage>804</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8938712</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="IldefonseandBennett1991"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ildefonse</surname><given-names>M.</given-names></name><name><surname>Bennett</surname><given-names>N.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Single-channel study of the cGMP-dependent conductance of retinal rods from incorporation of native vesicles into planar lipid bilayers</article-title><source>J. Membr. Biol.</source><volume>123</volume><year>1991</year><fpage>133</fpage><lpage>147</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1720176</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="JanandJan1990"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Jan</surname><given-names>L.Y.</given-names></name><name><surname>Jan</surname><given-names>Y.N.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>A superfamily of ion channels</article-title><source>Nature</source><volume>345</volume><year>1990</year><fpage>672</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1694264</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="KarlinandAkabas1998"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Karlin</surname><given-names>A.</given-names></name><name><surname>Akabas</surname><given-names>M.H.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Substituted-cysteine-accessibility method</article-title><person-group person-group-type="editor"><name><surname>Conn</surname><given-names>P.M.</given-names></name></person-group><source>In Methods in Enzymology</source><year>1998</year><fpage>123</fpage><lpage>136</lpage><publisher-name>Academic Press, Inc</publisher-name><publisher-loc>San Diego, CA</publisher-loc></citation></ref><ref id="Karpenetal1993"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Karpen</surname><given-names>J.W.</given-names></name><name><surname>Brown</surname><given-names>R.L.</given-names></name><name><surname>Stryer</surname><given-names>L.</given-names></name><name><surname>Baylor</surname><given-names>D.A.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Interactions between divalent cations and the gating machinery of cyclic GMP&#x02013;activated channels in salamander retinal rods</article-title><source>J. Gen. Physiol.</source><volume>101</volume><year>1993</year><fpage>1</fpage><lpage>25</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7679715</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="KarplusandPetsko1990"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Karplus</surname><given-names>M.</given-names></name><name><surname>Petsko</surname><given-names>G.A.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Molecular dynamics simulations in biology</article-title><source>Nature</source><volume>347</volume><year>1990</year><fpage>631</fpage><lpage>639</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2215695</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="Kauppetal1989"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kaupp</surname><given-names>U.B.</given-names></name><name><surname>Niidome</surname><given-names>T.</given-names></name><name><surname>Tanabe</surname><given-names>T.</given-names></name><name><surname>Terada</surname><given-names>S.</given-names></name><name><surname>Bonigk</surname><given-names>W.</given-names></name><name><surname>St&#x000fc;hmer</surname><given-names>W.</given-names></name><name><surname>Cook</surname><given-names>N.J.</given-names></name><name><surname>Kangawa</surname><given-names>K.</given-names></name><name><surname>Matsuo</surname><given-names>H.</given-names></name><name><surname>Hirose</surname><given-names>T.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Primary structure and functional expression from complementary DNA of the rod photoreceptor cyclic GMP&#x02013;gated channel</article-title><source>Nature.</source><volume>342</volume><year>1989</year><fpage>762</fpage><lpage>766</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2481236</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="Kaupp1995"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kaupp</surname><given-names>U.B.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Family of cyclic nucleotide gated ion channels</article-title><source>Curr. Opin. Neurobiol.</source><volume>5</volume><year>1995</year><fpage>434</fpage><lpage>442</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7488843</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="Kuneretal1996"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kuner</surname><given-names>T.</given-names></name><name><surname>Wollmuth</surname><given-names>L.P.</given-names></name><name><surname>Karlin</surname><given-names>A.</given-names></name><name><surname>Seeburg</surname><given-names>P.H.</given-names></name><name><surname>Sakmann</surname><given-names>B.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Structure of the NMDA receptor channel M2 segment inferred from the accessibility of substituted cysteines</article-title><source>Neuron.</source><volume>17</volume><year>1996</year><fpage>343</fpage><lpage>352</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8780657</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="Kurtzetal1995"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kurtz</surname><given-names>L.L.</given-names></name><name><surname>Zuhlke</surname><given-names>R.D.</given-names></name><name><surname>Zhang</surname><given-names>H.-J.</given-names></name><name><surname>Joho</surname><given-names>R.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Side-chain accessibilities in the pore of a K<sup>+</sup> channel probed by sulfhydryl-specific reagents after cysteine-scanning mutagenesis</article-title><source>Biophys. J.</source><volume>68</volume><year>1995</year><fpage>900</fpage><lpage>905</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7756555</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="LuandMiller1995"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Lu</surname><given-names>Q.</given-names></name><name><surname>Miller</surname><given-names>C.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Silver as a probe of pore-forming residues in a potassium channel</article-title><source>Science</source><volume>268</volume><year>1995</year><fpage>304</fpage><lpage>307</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7716526</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="Nizzarietal1993"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Nizzari</surname><given-names>M.</given-names></name><name><surname>Sesti</surname><given-names>F.</given-names></name><name><surname>Giraudo</surname><given-names>M.T.</given-names></name><name><surname>Virginio</surname><given-names>C.</given-names></name><name><surname>Cattaneo</surname><given-names>A.</given-names></name><name><surname>Torre</surname><given-names>V.</given-names></name></pers